# Claim 1

A method for forming metal bumps on a semiconductor substrate, comprising:

providing a semiconductor substrate having a first side and a second side opposite the first side, the semiconductor substrate including a plurality of first-side bond pads disposed on the first side and a plurality of second-side bond pads disposed on the second side;

forming a first under bump metallization (UBM) layer over the first side of the semiconductor substrate, the first UBM layer electrically contacting the plurality of first-side bond pads;

forming a first patterned mask layer over the first UBM layer, the first patterned mask layer defining a plurality of first bump openings exposing portions of the first UBM layer corresponding to the plurality of first-side bond pads;

depositing a first bump metal within the plurality of first bump openings to form a plurality of first-side metal bumps electrically coupled to the first UBM layer;

removing the first patterned mask layer to expose remaining portions of the first UBM layer not covered by the plurality of first-side metal bumps;

removing the exposed remaining portions of the first UBM layer to electrically isolate the plurality of first-side metal bumps from one another;

forming a second UBM layer over the second side of the semiconductor substrate, the second UBM layer electrically contacting the plurality of second-side bond pads;

forming a second patterned mask layer over the second UBM layer, the second patterned mask layer defining a plurality of second bump openings exposing portions of the second UBM layer corresponding to the plurality of second-side bond pads;

depositing a second bump metal within the plurality of second bump openings to form a plurality of second-side metal bumps electrically coupled to the second UBM layer;

removing the second patterned mask layer to expose remaining portions of the second UBM layer not covered by the plurality of second-side metal bumps;

removing the exposed remaining portions of the second UBM layer to electrically isolate the plurality of second-side metal bumps from one another; and

reflowing the plurality of first-side metal bumps and the plurality of second-side metal bumps to form substantially rounded first-side and second-side solder bumps on the semiconductor substrate.

**Claim 1**

A method of packaging a semiconductor device, the method comprising:

providing a semiconductor substrate having a front side and a back side opposite the front side, the front side comprising a plurality of conductive pads;

depositing a first under bump metallization (UBM) layer over the front side of the semiconductor substrate, the first UBM layer being in electrical contact with the plurality of conductive pads;

depositing a second UBM layer over the back side of the semiconductor substrate;

forming a plurality of bumps on the first UBM layer over the front side of the semiconductor substrate;

after forming the plurality of bumps, removing portions of the first UBM layer not disposed beneath the plurality of bumps and removing the second UBM layer from the back side of the semiconductor substrate; and

reflowing the plurality of bumps to form a plurality of solder bumps electrically coupled to the plurality of conductive pads.
